# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles run inside Linux containers -- CRLF line
# endings (this repo is worked on from Windows, and git's core.autocrlf can
# rewrite these on checkout/commit) break shebang parsing and shell syntax.
# Force LF regardless of platform for anything that ends up inside a container.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# CSVs are data exports, some of them restore sources (ops/release-*/articles-*.csv
# are \copy'd back into Postgres by reverse.sql). Keep them byte-for-byte: CRLF
# conversion would put \r into multi-line headlines/summaries on restore.
*.csv -text
